<title>UK: BRITAIN-ABBEY.</title>
<headline>BRITAIN-ABBEY.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Abbey National Plc kicked off the bank reporting season on Tuesday with a 23 percent rise in pre-tax profits to 687 million pounds ($1.1 billion) in the six months to June 30.</p>
<p>Abbey said it will maintain its progressive dividend policy and announced a 17 percent increase for the first half to 10.2 pence per share.</p>
</text>
